{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: b424b752e0d822d32c316306f0ac03fe32a5cdaf (request/merge-plan-review-repair-3 tip, origin matches; four commits over current main 4db60847; Rests-On fd6d8c2f; all fifteen cited artifacts at this head covering the fifteen changed destinations, cmd/gs covering the deleted succession_test.go). The first three commits are a faithful rebase of the reviewed ac2b28dc: their tree differs from it only by main's own two-file delta. Gates at the head with -count=1: gofmt, git diff --check, go mod verify, make build, make vet, go test ./... (one timing test, TestWhoamiBoundsStallsAndRejectsRedirects, failed once while a concurrent mutation batch ran and passed on a quiet rerun of the whole cmd/gitseq-mcp package), make docs rerun uncached, tree clean. The previous blocker is repaired and proven: Build validates succession against the disposable staged clone (mergeplan.go:1241-1269, 1342-1376), and the two new fixtures diverge the trees as required. TestMergeBareRetirementOfACitedPredecessorLeavesTargetUnchanged (main_test.go:2331) now uses workflowCandidateAddsCitation, asserts docs/reference/base.md is absent on the target and present on the candidate, and requires succession_refused naming that page; TestMergePlanAllowsCandidateThatDeletesTheSoleCitation (2375) commits the page on the target, removes it on the candidate, and requires Build to allow. Passing the target checkout to ValidateSuccession, or resetting the clone's tree to the target after the diff, is killed by both. The redundant post-staging preflightSuccession is removed from mergeCommand and merge.md:392-400 describes the actual sequence; succession recording still validates the landed checkout (succession.go:145). Both new pages list five classifications including carried, matching Classify. refuseUnreachableCrossAuthorRetirements, reviewedPaths and the leftLive constants are gone from cmd/gs. DecisionEffective, StandingStatement, LiveStatementAsOf, StandingArtifact and LiveArtifactAsOf are now one exported implementation in mergeplan with no copies left in cmd/gs; breaking each is killed by cmd/gs tests. The early validateMerge phase is pinned by eight error-precedence tests and the late one is what evaluates --authorization and feeds Staleness and the ratification witness into the receipt. The three coherence guards remain killed by their tests. Architecture: layers internal/mergeplan (evaluation), cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp (surfaces), internal/app (citation guard and read-only act building), documentation. The head moves the sole pre-commit citation site into the evaluator and deletes the command-side duplicate; architecture.md:1286-1295 and merge.md are accurate for it, and the contract stated there is preserved. Security: candidate is a canonical full object ID before any git call, -- separators throughout, the clone is --shared --no-checkout under a random MkdirTemp and writes only there, cleanup runs on every error path and by defer on success, Build appends and reserves nothing, authorization is evaluated only in gs merge, Classify fails closed, and the fail-closed citation lookup now provably reads the staged tree. No unresolved security defect. Two follow-ups filed as a child request rather than blocking: user-global core.hooksPath hooks run inside the disposable clone during checkout, so the read-only surface should pass -c core.hooksPath= to its clone, checkout and merge; and internal/mergeplan has no unit tests of its own liveness helpers, so their mutations pass the package suite and are caught only by cmd/gs. Simplification: about 110 lines of duplication and dead helpers are gone; remaining and noted for later, uniqueStandingBasis in main.go is dead, reviewguard.StandingArtifact/StandingStatement duplicate mergeplan's, and the early validateMerge phase buys only error precedence at the cost of a third fold. Approved for merge of this exact head only; any change returns it to implementation.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d